            For most homes, the Snow Joe RJ208M is the best roof rake: long reach, a debris slide and wheels that keep it off the shingles. Choose the Avalanche! 500 for a fiberglass pole on a single-story asphalt roof, the Avalanche! 750 for metal, tile or solar, the Snow Joe RJ204M or Suncast for a light pull rake, the SNOWPEELER for the most reach and the ROOF-RAZOR for deep snow.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whichever you buy, rake from the ground, look up for power lines before you extend the pole, stand back from falling snow, leave an inch or two on the shingles and never chip at ice dams.
